            "body": "## Foundry MCP Server v0.8.4\n\nComplete multi-platform distribution for Foundry MCP Server - AI-powered campaign management for Foundry VTT using Claude Desktop.\n\n**Compatible with Foundry VTT v13 and v14.**\n\n### Installation Options\n\n**Windows Users:**\n- Download `FoundryMCPServer-Setup-v0.8.4.exe`\n- Run installer (no admin rights required)\n- Automatic Claude Desktop configuration\n\n**Mac Users:**\n- Download `FoundryMCPServer-v0.8.4.dmg`\n- Open DMG and double-click the PKG installer\n- Choose components: MCP Server (required), Foundry Module, ComfyUI AI Maps\n- Automatic Claude Desktop configuration\n- To uninstall: Double-click `Uninstall.tool` from the DMG\n\n**Manual Installation (All Platforms):**\n- Download `foundry-mcp-server-v0.8.4.zip`\n- Extract and run with Node.js 18+\n- Manual Claude Desktop configuration required\n\n**Foundry VTT Users:**\n- Install directly from Foundry's module browser\n- Or use manifest: `https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/releases/latest/download/module.json`\n\n### Quick Start\n1. Choose your installation method above\n2. Install MCP Bridge module in Foundry VTT\n3. Restart Claude Desktop\n4. Start creating AI-powered campaigns!\n\n### New in this release\n- Scene music and playlist tools: bind playlists and tracks to scenes, plus playlist CRUD and playback control\n- ActiveEffect management: create, update and delete effects on actors or their items\n- DSA5 system support, plus a new `replace-journal-page` tool\n- `manage-actors` can now place existing world actors onto the current scene\n- Fixes: `use-item` targeting on Foundry V13/V14, Windows installer upgrade safety (no longer risks an existing ComfyUI install), large responses timing out over WebRTC, and several D&D 5e feature-creation defects\n\nSee the changelog for the full list.\n\n### Features\n- 48 MCP tools for comprehensive Foundry VTT integration\n- Multi-system support: D&D 5e, Pathfinder 2e, DSA5, Cosmere RPG, WFRP4e, and Mongoose Traveller 2e\n- Generic actor CRUD (create/update/delete actors and embedded items) across all systems\n- D&D 5e NPC creation suite: stat blocks, attacks, saves, auras, and spellcasting\n- Actor creation with natural language processing\n- Quest management with HTML generation and updates\n- Campaign system with multi-part structure and progress tracking\n- Dice roll coordination between Claude and Foundry players\n- Actor ownership management with bulk operations\n- Enhanced creature index for instant monster searches\n- AI-powered battlemap generation with ComfyUI integration\n\nFor full documentation, visit: https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp\n\n\n## What's Changed\n* chore: correct release-notes tool count and system list by @adambdooley in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/71\n* ci: guard against version drift across manifests by @adambdooley in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/72\n* fix: repair scene background image after generate-map scene creation by @Sir-Salty-Bacon in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/79\n* fix(module): use ws:// for loopback hosts even on HTTPS pages (#74) by @adambdooley in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/82\n* feat: DSA5 adapter support (normalizePayload, describeActorSchema) + system detection + replace-journal-page tool by @frankyh75 in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/81\n* fix: include scene_name in map job dedup hash (#80) by @adambdooley in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/84\n* fix: register getPackIndex query for list-dsa5-archetypes (#77) by @adambdooley in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/83\n* feat: add 'place' action to manage-actors for existing world actors (#75) by @adambdooley in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/85\n* fix: scope .form-footer rules to the module's own settings forms by @apoapostolov in https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/pull/97\n* Fix/journal page rename (Issue #95) by @tacostorm in https://github.com/adambd"
          }
        ],
        "manifest_url": "https://github.com/adambdooley/foundry-vtt-mcp/releases/latest/download/module.json"
      },
